sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/coupled-model-v2-real-fish-cannot-reach-liftoff-from-physiology-power> a delphi:Hypothesis, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Driven by its modelled physiology alone, a 60 g flying fish cannot reach lift-off speed in the coupled model, and its aerobic power is two orders of magnitude short of powered flight" ;
    dct:description "Simulator version 2, pre-registered before any run (physics/sim/PREREG-v2.md, sha256 2dde1f61f3aa65ebd116bbad302d61419cf4c7198cdccbbc5e3a05def8056828): swim and taxi thrust come only from the physiology chain's axial power (aerobic plus burst), with the body water drag kept as a named assumption (no fetched coefficient; logged search epmc-v2-fish-drag) and swept from C_d 0.03 to 0.3; sustained powered flight defined in advance as aerobic-only net mechanical energy gain held for 10 s. Result: the real fish never becomes airborne in any arm; peak speed 10.0 m/s at C_d 0.1, 13.7 at 0.03, 7.3 at 0.3, against about 16 m/s needed for its fins to lift it under the run-6 trim law and measured polar; the burst store empties in the attempt. Test 4 v2 is therefore recorded as not reachable under these assumptions, neither passed nor failed, as the pre-registration provided. Independently of reachability, the chain's aerobic flight power for a bat-sized flight muscle (9.13 percent of body mass, red fibres 5 percent of it at the scup red-muscle maximum of 134 W/kg at 20 C, Q10 1.88) is 0.009 W against 1.44 W required for level flight. Status: inconclusive for the test; the power shortfall is a supported statement about the model." ;
    delphi:context "Claim under test: thompson1917-ch02-06 (D Arcy Thompson 1917, On Growth and Form, ch. II, Project Gutenberg 55264 lines 1716-1790), with thompson1917-ch02-07 and thompson1917-ch02-10. Taxon: Exocoetidae, NCBI Taxonomy 76072, GBIF 2968. Class Aves is the frozen holdout (holdout/exam.json); no bird value enters this record." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-simulator-v2-runs> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1242/jeb.046052>, <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06032-9> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Simulated throughout; the pre-registration fixed the launch model, the definition of sustained flight, the arms and the sweep before any run." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: inconclusive. Does not establish: that a real flying fish cannot reach 15 to 20 m/s (it does, in the field); it establishes that the model's assumed water drag, assumed lobe thrust model, or the chain's burst-store proxy (mahi-mahi), or more than one, are wrong for this fish, in that order of suspicion; which one is not decided here. Does not establish anything about birds. The v1 record (test 4 passed at own muscle, failed at the post-hoc upper bound) stands unchanged." ;
    rdfs:comment "Pre-registration: physics/tests/thompson1917-ch02-06/result.json, written 2026-10-31T18:21:00Z before any wing loading, lifting area or lift coefficient was read, amended 2026-10-31T18:26:00Z before any fit ran (the file lists both and the values seen before each); sha256 at build 0094c084db22278a5f98d96cc2971ccd27813b0acdc458d60cadf7c7b7bcae48. The git commit that timestamps it is pending: the physics thread does not commit; the hub does." ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-06> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-simulator-v2-runs> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Version-2 runs (a), (b), (c) and the drag sweep, 90 s each, headless" ;
    dct:description "physics/sim/RUNS.md, v2 section: (a) fmf 0: not airborne, peak 10.0 m/s; (b) fmf 0.0913 flapping from total power: not airborne, aerobic flight power max 0.009 W, no burst bout; (c) fmf 0.0913 flapping from aerobic power: not airborne; sweep C_d 0.03 peak 13.7 m/s, C_d 0.3 peak 7.3 m/s; burst store 0 percent and blood O2 store 25 to 28 percent at the end of each. Physiology copy sha256-identical to the committed physiology/. Flags v2=1, flapsrc, fmf, cdw, tmax as pre-registered; nothing tuned." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/coupled-model-v2-real-fish-cannot-reach-liftoff-from-physiology-power> ;
    rdfs:comment "Computed by physics/analysis.py from physics/glide-data.csv (sha256 bc24245b5163723b192e95fccf714ef6e4b3b28e71df4fef3befbaf008a00635) and physics/comparison-data.csv (sha256 e0d3d74639c1fe856fe5128c1783151596fde3acc923a2409be3d3f870cc394a); numbers in physics/results.json (sha256 63336841c0d4c9ae2760ae5c87a9251b97218e3ebfdd453cad4cffb9cdf6ba0b). Every input value carries its source, locator, retrieval time and value kind in those files." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/glide-data.csv>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/comparison-data.csv> .
}

